[0.8.7]
- update readme regarding token settings

[0.8.6]
- Revert: client-side error message formatting (caused raw JSON parse errors to surface)
- Note: if you see auth errors, recreate your Personal Access Token in Firefly-III
  (Profile → OAuth → Personal Access Tokens)

[0.8.5]
- Fix: proxy now detects when Firefly-III redirects to login (expired/invalid token)
  and returns a clear HTTP 401 instead of a confusing JSON parse error
- Fix: guard against non-JSON responses from misconfigured reverse proxies
- Fix: error messages now include the Node.js error code (e.g. ECONNREFUSED),
  the target URL, and the raw detail — making connection issues actionable
- Chore: remove unused SESSION_SECRET from .env.example
